WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.500
The Star Wars universe is vast and infinitely
rich in lore, with just about every minor

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.540
background character having their own book,
action figure, and fanfic page.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.800
It can all get a bit overwhelming for the
average fan, which is why we've put together

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.990
this quick guide to some of the new Rogue
One characters with more meaning than you

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.420
realize.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.600
Tivik

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.740
While you're toasting the destruction of the
Death Star, stop and pour out a 40 for poor

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:25.740
Tivik.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.119
If you don't recognize the name, Tivik is
the Rebel informant who passes word to Cassian

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:32.200
Andor about Bodhi's secret message.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.710
Andor repays Tivik by slaying him.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.130
It's a surprisingly dark move for a member
of the heroic Rebel Alliance, which in previous

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:42.380
films had been painted as the white knights
of the galaxy.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.489
Cassian's ruthless decision to slay Tivik
in order to ensure the secrecy of his mission

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:51.480
paints the Alliance in a far more morally
ambiguous light, and sets the tone for the

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.640
entire film by letting the audience know right
away that this isn't your parents' shiny,

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.770
happy Rebellion.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:00.890
With both the plot and the tone of the movie
turning on Tivik, his one short scene holds

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:03.210
an unusual amount of meaning.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.529
Weeteef Cyubee

00:01:04.529 --> 00:01:09.789
This guy has very little backstory so far,
but Weeteef Cyubee's presence among Saw Gerrera's

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:13.369
Partisans speaks to the variety of the Empire's
misdeeds.

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:18.200
If this little trigger-happy piranha-looking
dude hates the Empire enough to fight, main,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.779
and die on the side of the Rebels, then the
Empire might want to consider re-evaluating

00:01:22.779 --> 00:01:24.279
its outreach policy.

00:01:24.279 --> 00:01:28.319
Given what we know of the Ewoks' future role
in bringing down the Empire, it would seem

00:01:28.319 --> 00:01:32.709
that the Empire's policies either discriminate
against or simply don't account for vertically

00:01:32.709 --> 00:01:34.049
challenged species.

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:37.750
And that's not the only connection between
Weeteef and the Ewoks: Weeteef was played

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.460
by Warwick Davis, who also played Wicket in
Return of the Jedi.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.300
(Cute Ewok sound)

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.040
Beezer Fortuna

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:51.389
Related to Jabba the Hutt's right-hand man
Bib Fortuna, Beezer is another member of the

00:01:51.389 --> 00:01:52.389
Partisans.

00:01:52.389 --> 00:01:56.679
The fate of Beezer, who was seen briefly at
Saw Gerrera's hideout on Jedha, is unclear,

00:01:56.679 --> 00:02:00.249
but his connection to Bib Fortuna speaks to
Saw Gerrera's willingness to work with the

00:02:00.249 --> 00:02:02.850
criminal underworld to bring down the Empire.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:07.540
Too bad we didn't get to see the two Fortunas
settle their ideological differences — through

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.319
a desert dance-off!.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:12.140
KX-Series Security Droid

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.400
The KX-Series Security Droid is a product
line of Arakyd Industries, a company whose

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.980
connection to the Galactic Empire runs deep.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.959
The KX-Series clearly has some serious security
issues, which allowed Cassian Andor to reprogram

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:25.590
K-2SO to the good side.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.680
"I'll be there for you.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.659
The captain said I had to."

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:34.030
Despite this, though, Arakyd Industries remains
partnered with the Empire throughout the original

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.160
trilogy.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.460
They're the folks responsible for the iconic
Viper probe droids that hunt down Luke Skywalker

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.260
and Han Solo on the ice planet Hoth in The
Empire Strikes Back.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.400
Why would the Empire keep working with a company
which makes dangerously shoddy droids that

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.820
can be easily hacked, or taken out with one
shot?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:55.040
Probably because Grand Moff Tarkin inadvertently
destroyed the evidence of their droids' vulnerabilities

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.290
when he blew up Scariff base.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.400
Whoops!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.739
Thanks for watching!

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:02.359
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:02.359 --> 00:03:04.400
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

